A||N||24||AusFiero||Gauge Faces are go go go - OEM quality or better||||6||
Z||000000||AusFiero||07-25-2001||10:41 PM||||Om I couldn't help myself. I rang my printer. Who in turn had done his research as requested and being the good bloke he is he told me many ways he could do it, but felt it could still be better. But being a real fair guy and knowing I want the best quality product on the market he researched further and found an associate that makes the OEM gauge faces for some of the Aussie car manufacturers. <P>So tomorrow I have a meeting with the guy about making gauge faces for me. The quality will be the same or better as any GM or any car manufacturers gauge faces that is released in current model cars. <P>He can also do my custom one offs for very little extra as he is tooled up big time for this sort of stuff specifically. <P>Almost any colour will be available, as will a huge variety of backlit colour choices. <P>Not to end there though he also discussed how to make the exisiting lighting behind the panel better than original to get that modern car glow that gauge panels really should do. He has put me onto a guy that should be able to produce new lighting kits to replace all your factory crappy lights (lets face it they are crap) with a modern alternative that will make you your new backlight colours bright and vibrant and totally consistant just like any new car, unlike most Fiero gauge panel lights now. Him I will ring next week. <P>We haven't talked prices as yet as volume will determine that. But we have talked quality. Just think New Car, New Gauges and you got the look.<P>OK I will rest now as I said I would.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||6
